<title>USA: Avid says Media 100 suit dismissed.</title>
<headline>Avid says Media 100 suit dismissed.</headline>
<dateline>TEWKSBURY, Mass. 1997-05-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Avid Technology Inc said Thursday that a patent infringement suit brought against it by Media 100 Inc, formerly known as Data Translation Inc, has been dismissed, by agreement of the two companies.</p>
<p>The suit, filed in April 1966, was dismissed with prejudice and as such, Media 100 may not sue Avid over the same patent involving Avid products at issue in the case, Avid said.  </p>
<p>It said the dismissal of the case does not involve any of the parties paying any consideration.</p>
<p>Avid said the dismissal of the suit does not affect its patent infringement suit against Media 100, which is pending in a Massachussetts federal court.</p>
</text>
